1
00:00:28,438 --> 00:00:29,708
Still not home yet?

2
00:00:30,168 --> 00:00:32,008
I was hoping to talk about the site selection.

3
00:00:44,788 --> 00:00:45,788
Father.

4
00:00:47,118 --> 00:00:49,018
Team Leader Ko, are you just back from work?

5
00:00:49,118 --> 00:00:52,088
Yes. I was preparing for Grandfather's event with Eun Ae.

6
00:00:52,588 --> 00:00:54,158
What brings you to this room?

7
00:00:54,498 --> 00:00:55,498
Well...

8
00:00:55,698 --> 00:00:58,368
I compiled a list of suitable sites for Team Two.

9
00:00:58,428 --> 00:00:59,998
I came to give you this, but...

10
00:01:01,238 --> 00:01:04,638
Oh, I see. Thank you for being so thoughtful.

11
00:01:05,838 --> 00:01:06,838
Is this person...

12
00:01:07,908 --> 00:01:09,548
your father, Team Leader Ko?

13
00:01:10,478 --> 00:01:11,478
Yes.

14
00:01:12,748 --> 00:01:14,878
So your father worked at Gangsu Construction.

15
00:01:17,188 --> 00:01:21,288
But he looks so familiar.

16
00:01:21,888 --> 00:01:22,888
Really?

17
00:01:25,228 --> 00:01:29,428
I guess it's because you look so much like your father.

18
00:01:30,328 --> 00:01:31,368
I suppose so.

19
00:01:31,728 --> 00:01:34,238
Seeing him in a picture with the Chairman like that,

20
00:01:34,298 --> 00:01:37,608
he must have been a special employee to the Chairman.

21
00:01:37,768 --> 00:01:39,408
Yes. I heard my father was...

22
00:01:39,478 --> 00:01:41,578
the first scholarship recipient from Gangsu Construction.

23
00:01:42,138 --> 00:01:43,778
After college, he worked for ten years...

24
00:01:43,848 --> 00:01:46,048
on Gangsu Construction's architectural design team.

25
00:01:46,548 --> 00:01:47,948
I see.

26
00:01:49,178 --> 00:01:51,718
It's late. Go wash up and get to bed.

27
00:01:51,948 --> 00:01:54,618
- Yes. Good night, Father. - Okay. You too.

28
00:02:03,898 --> 00:02:04,898
Father.

29
00:02:05,798 --> 00:02:07,798
That was the little kid's father.

30
00:02:09,198 --> 00:02:11,738
He treats me like his own son.

31
00:02:13,778 --> 00:02:15,078
Bringing me here...

32
00:02:16,708 --> 00:02:18,408
it's all thanks to you, isn't it?

33
00:02:21,948 --> 00:02:23,518
I went to the police station today.

34
00:02:24,688 --> 00:02:27,058
That day that's been completely erased...

35
00:02:27,118 --> 00:02:28,118
from my memory,

36
00:02:29,158 --> 00:02:31,958
I'm curious about what exactly happened.

37
00:02:34,158 --> 00:02:36,998
I hope that's okay.

38
00:02:40,538 --> 00:02:42,398
Like this, like this.

39
00:02:42,868 --> 00:02:46,108
Our Bit Na is so good at cat's cradle.

40
00:02:49,308 --> 00:02:50,608
It's Mom.

41
00:02:51,178 --> 00:02:52,278
Mom.

42
00:02:52,608 --> 00:02:54,778
Bit Na, what are you doing?

43
00:02:55,248 --> 00:02:57,248
I was playing cat's cradle with Grandma.

44
00:02:57,548 --> 00:03:00,458
I'm good at cat's cradle. Where are you, Mom?

45
00:03:00,518 --> 00:03:02,588
I just finished my flight and got to my place...

46
00:03:02,658 --> 00:03:03,658
a little while ago.

47
00:03:04,358 --> 00:03:05,388
Are you in Grandma's room?

48
00:03:05,688 --> 00:03:08,198
Yes. Grandma's right here. I'll put her on.

49
00:03:09,428 --> 00:03:10,928
No. Bit Na, wait...

50
00:03:11,498 --> 00:03:13,968
Why? You don't even want to talk to me anymore?

51
00:03:15,268 --> 00:03:16,308
No, Mother.

52
00:03:17,038 --> 00:03:21,178
- That's not it. Have you been well? - Of course, I've been well.

53
00:03:21,678 --> 00:03:23,308
Your place? Where is it?

54
00:03:23,778 --> 00:03:26,918
I got a studio apartment near the airport.

55
00:03:27,178 --> 00:03:28,748
Someplace convenient for my commute.

56
00:03:29,448 --> 00:03:32,248
- I'm sorry, Mother. - What do you have to be sorry for?

57
00:03:32,588 --> 00:03:35,558
Come by the house sometime for a meal.

58
00:03:35,888 --> 00:03:37,258
Take care of yourself.

59
00:03:37,328 --> 00:03:40,258
Yes, Mother. Please put Bit Na back on.

60
00:03:42,728 --> 00:03:46,438
Mom, I have a great-grandmother now. And a great-grandfather too.

61
00:03:46,668 --> 00:03:49,538
A great-grandmother and great-grandfather?

62
00:03:50,568 --> 00:03:53,408
She's Grandma's mom. We went to greet them today.

63
00:03:53,808 --> 00:03:54,808
Oh, really?

64
00:03:55,738 --> 00:03:58,548
Okay, Bit Na. I'll make time to visit you soon.

65
00:03:58,908 --> 00:04:02,518
- It's late, so go to sleep now. - Okay. Good night, Mom.

66
00:04:04,618 --> 00:04:05,918
You're so lucky, Bit Na,

67
00:04:05,988 --> 00:04:08,018
that you'll get to see your mom often.

68
00:04:08,218 --> 00:04:10,828
Yes, it's great. Grandma, Grandpa.

69
00:04:11,258 --> 00:04:13,798
- Good night. - Okay, sleep well.

70
00:04:13,858 --> 00:04:17,068
Okay, sleep well, our Bit Na. Come on, sleep.

71
00:04:17,568 --> 00:04:19,398
- Here, lie down. - Yes, lie down.

72
00:04:23,338 --> 00:04:25,038
- Oh, right. This. - What?

73
00:04:25,668 --> 00:04:26,678
Oh my.

74
00:04:29,508 --> 00:04:30,808
What in the world is this?

75
00:04:35,348 --> 00:04:38,088
You're Invited to My Funeral.

76
00:04:39,088 --> 00:04:41,858
Lest we regret the words left unsaid after I'm gone,

77
00:04:42,288 --> 00:04:45,188
I've arranged this gathering a little early.

78
00:04:46,198 --> 00:04:49,027
Earlier today, I took Eun Hyung, Eun Nim, and Bit Na...

79
00:04:49,028 --> 00:04:50,598
to the Chairman's house.

80
00:04:50,668 --> 00:04:51,698
He gave me this.

81
00:04:53,298 --> 00:04:55,038
Oh, it's just heartbreaking.

82
00:04:55,868 --> 00:04:57,538
No matter how much I try to think of it...

83
00:04:57,608 --> 00:04:58,608
as a happy occasion.

84
00:04:59,138 --> 00:05:00,138
I know.

85
00:05:01,208 --> 00:05:02,438
Of course you'd feel that way.

86
00:05:02,838 --> 00:05:05,178
But since the Chairman is so firm in his decision,

87
00:05:05,248 --> 00:05:07,478
we have to be as bright and cheerful as possible for him.

88
00:05:07,548 --> 00:05:08,548
What else can we do?

89
00:05:09,248 --> 00:05:11,618
You're right. My mother is taking it calmly, too.

90
00:05:12,418 --> 00:05:14,058
By the way, didn't you say you had something...

91
00:05:14,118 --> 00:05:15,118
to give Team Leader Ko?

92
00:05:15,218 --> 00:05:16,728
Oh, I gave it to him a little while ago.

93
00:05:17,758 --> 00:05:20,958
But when I saw the photo of his biological father...

94
00:05:21,028 --> 00:05:22,028
on his desk...

95
00:05:23,528 --> 00:05:26,698
I couldn't shake the feeling that he looked strangely familiar.

96
00:05:26,998 --> 00:05:30,038
So the picture on his desk was of his father.

97
00:05:30,938 --> 00:05:34,008
- Why? Does he look familiar? - What?

98
00:05:34,378 --> 00:05:35,778
Maybe.

99
00:05:36,908 --> 00:05:39,917
But Team Leader Ko seems to be going through a lot lately.

100
00:05:39,918 --> 00:05:41,248
Haven't you noticed?

101
00:05:42,178 --> 00:05:45,648
Now that you mention it, he has seemed a bit worn out lately.

102
00:05:46,758 --> 00:05:50,058
He must have relied on his grandfather so much,

103
00:05:50,358 --> 00:05:52,858
maybe it's because of the upcoming living funeral.

104
00:05:53,358 --> 00:05:54,358
That's probably it, right?

105
00:05:55,128 --> 00:05:57,868
All the more reason for us to be warm and supportive.

106
00:05:59,738 --> 00:06:01,368
Of course. We should.

107
00:06:02,168 --> 00:06:05,408
Go to sleep first. I'm going to knit a bit more.

108
00:06:07,538 --> 00:06:09,848
Oh, for one reason or another...

109
00:06:10,448 --> 00:06:11,808
I can't seem to fall asleep.

110
00:06:12,778 --> 00:06:14,748
(You're Invited to My Happy Funeral)

111
00:06:24,928 --> 00:06:26,188
Do you have much left to do?

112
00:06:26,258 --> 00:06:28,698
No, I'll be there soon. You go to sleep first.

113
00:06:29,198 --> 00:06:34,038
- Is something on your mind lately? - Me? No.

114
00:06:34,738 --> 00:06:36,468
What do I have to worry about?

115
00:06:38,068 --> 00:06:40,478
It's just that looking at this makes my heart a bit heavy.

116
00:06:42,678 --> 00:06:43,678
Oh, my goodness.

117
00:06:44,978 --> 00:06:47,148
While he was writing this invitation by hand,

118
00:06:47,918 --> 00:06:49,578
I wonder what he must have been feeling.

119
00:06:52,248 --> 00:06:55,658
We should prepare a gift, but what should we get him?

120
00:06:55,858 --> 00:06:58,628
He specifically asked us to come empty-handed.

121
00:06:58,858 --> 00:07:00,298
I know, but still.

122
00:07:00,758 --> 00:07:03,198
Instead of a gift, we should show him our sincerity.

123
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,698
Show him how much he means to us.

124
00:07:07,138 --> 00:07:09,738
You're right. I'm going to sleep first,

125
00:07:10,068 --> 00:07:12,268
- so come to bed soon. - Okay.

126
00:07:19,278 --> 00:07:22,948
Do you happen to know anything about my father's accident?

127
00:07:23,018 --> 00:07:25,748
What kind of accident it was and how it happened.

128
00:07:26,318 --> 00:07:27,887
President Ko already has his own son,

129
00:07:27,888 --> 00:07:29,517
so I'm curious why he'd go out of his way...

130
00:07:29,518 --> 00:07:30,758
to adopt Team Leader Ko.

131
00:07:32,128 --> 00:07:35,798
President Ko only agreed because the Chairman told him to.

132
00:07:36,928 --> 00:07:38,928
Was he the son of an acquaintance of the Chairman?

133
00:07:45,008 --> 00:07:47,808
So you're saying you'll honour Father's wishes?

134
00:07:49,108 --> 00:07:50,978
Of course. What else can we do?

135
00:07:52,278 --> 00:07:54,548
Let's prepare it properly.

136
00:07:55,318 --> 00:07:57,888
This is our last chance to show him how much we care.

137
00:07:57,948 --> 00:08:00,358
Yes, we need to prepare everything perfectly...

138
00:08:00,418 --> 00:08:01,858
and move Father so that...

139
00:08:02,018 --> 00:08:04,758
- the remaining 20 percent stake... - There you go again.

140
00:08:05,288 --> 00:08:07,298
Seriously, Crystal. That stake that's stuck...

141
00:08:07,358 --> 00:08:08,358
in your head,

142
00:08:08,428 --> 00:08:10,698
can't you just get it out of your mind for once?

143
00:08:11,168 --> 00:08:12,968
How am I supposed to forget it?

144
00:08:13,028 --> 00:08:15,468
It's not like I have an eraser in my head.

145
00:08:17,138 --> 00:08:22,078
- Who gets the 20 percent stake... - Snap out of it.

146
00:08:24,778 --> 00:08:29,148
- Oh, give me a break. - Honey, I'm serious this time.

147
00:08:29,248 --> 00:08:32,348
I'm going to hire a hotel chef and throw a proper party.

148
00:08:32,948 --> 00:08:34,988
Oh, should we sing a song for him together?

149
00:08:35,458 --> 00:08:37,358
We can hire a string ensemble to perform.

150
00:08:37,728 --> 00:08:40,458
You and I can get all dressed up in a tuxedo and a gown,

151
00:08:40,528 --> 00:08:41,528
what do you say?

152
00:08:42,098 --> 00:08:46,028
Okay, Crystal, I'm well aware of your deep devotion,

153
00:08:46,328 --> 00:08:47,798
but look at this invitation.

154
00:08:48,338 --> 00:08:50,608
Father wants to gather the people he wants to see,

155
00:08:50,668 --> 00:08:53,808
and have a small, simple event.

156
00:08:53,878 --> 00:08:56,408
It's all written right here in the invitation.

157
00:08:56,778 --> 00:09:00,878
What? That's just your interpretation. Here, look.

158
00:09:01,018 --> 00:09:03,318
It says this is supposed to be the brightest...

159
00:09:03,388 --> 00:09:07,688
and most joyful day of his life. "My Happy Funeral." Gosh.

160
00:09:10,658 --> 00:09:12,688
You're the chief mourner that day, got it?

161
00:09:12,758 --> 00:09:15,398
Don't let Secretary Jo or Manager Seo take your place.

162
00:09:15,458 --> 00:09:16,498
Assert yourself.

163
00:09:18,128 --> 00:09:20,098
Assert myself about what?

164
00:09:25,868 --> 00:09:27,138
There. All done.

165
00:09:27,638 --> 00:09:30,078
How do I look? Do I look okay?

166
00:09:30,448 --> 00:09:32,148
Yes, you look wonderful.

167
00:09:33,418 --> 00:09:36,788
You look like you could be a groom standing at the altar.

168
00:09:36,988 --> 00:09:40,918
Well then, let's just pretend we're the bride and groom.

169
00:09:42,288 --> 00:09:46,698
- Have all the guests arrived? - They're all here getting ready.

170
00:09:47,698 --> 00:09:50,328
As for the food, Yeon Soon...

171
00:09:50,668 --> 00:09:53,268
and Seung Ri's mom have been handling it perfectly,

172
00:09:53,338 --> 00:09:55,238
so there's been nothing for me to do.

173
00:09:58,108 --> 00:09:59,408
Lee Young Hwa.

174
00:10:00,778 --> 00:10:06,048
Today is the most joyful and happiest day of my life.

175
00:10:07,748 --> 00:10:08,748
Don't you dare...

176
00:10:09,278 --> 00:10:10,988
think about crying.

177
00:10:11,448 --> 00:10:14,018
Of course. I wouldn't dream of it.

178
00:10:15,718 --> 00:10:17,988
I'll be smiling a lot.

179
00:10:18,988 --> 00:10:21,128
Good. That's the spirit.

180
00:10:29,838 --> 00:10:33,008
The food is all served, so I think we're all ready.

181
00:10:33,608 --> 00:10:37,178
- Thanks for your hard work, ma'am. - Not at all. You worked hard too.

182
00:10:38,708 --> 00:10:42,178
- Thanks for your help, Yu Jung Ran. - Don't mention it.

183
00:10:42,748 --> 00:10:46,388
This is what I always used to do for the Chairman's events.

184
00:10:47,318 --> 00:10:48,988
I'm sorry about the other day.

185
00:10:49,058 --> 00:10:51,288
As a mother, I lost my cool for a moment,

186
00:10:51,488 --> 00:10:53,258
and I was too harsh.

187
00:10:53,598 --> 00:10:56,628
And I'm sorry for hitting your son's back.

188
00:10:57,268 --> 00:10:58,428
Please forgive me.

189
00:10:59,068 --> 00:11:00,068
Don't worry about it.

190
00:11:00,838 --> 00:11:02,267
If I were in your shoes, Kang Yeon Ja,

191
00:11:02,268 --> 00:11:06,708
- I would have lost my cool too. - No, I was completely in the wrong.

192
00:11:07,338 --> 00:11:08,338
If I cherish my own child,

193
00:11:08,408 --> 00:11:10,248
I should know how to cherish other people's children.

194
00:11:10,978 --> 00:11:14,448
- You really mean that, don't you? - Oh, of course.

195
00:11:15,218 --> 00:11:18,718
So, have we officially made up?

196
00:11:19,418 --> 00:11:22,058
What was there to make up about between us?

197
00:11:22,818 --> 00:11:23,928
Exactly.

198
00:11:24,428 --> 00:11:27,028
By the way, why haven't I seen Min Ho's Mom...

199
00:11:27,098 --> 00:11:28,098
all morning?

200
00:11:28,358 --> 00:11:31,068
She's probably planning to surprise us again.

201
00:11:31,468 --> 00:11:33,398
- Shall we go out too? - Yes.

202
00:11:39,508 --> 00:11:41,508
Oh, my, what's with you two?

203
00:11:41,778 --> 00:11:44,148
I mean, how can you come to a party in casual clothes?

204
00:11:44,778 --> 00:11:45,948
This is our idea of dressing up,

205
00:11:46,008 --> 00:11:47,548
so mind your own business and go on ahead.

206
00:11:47,878 --> 00:11:49,418
I'm going to escort these two out.

207
00:11:49,518 --> 00:11:53,458
What? Why are you escorting them?

208
00:11:53,518 --> 00:11:56,158
Well, of course. She's their daughter.

209
00:11:56,458 --> 00:11:57,458
Come on, let's go.

210
00:11:57,528 --> 00:11:59,228
Okay, I get it. Slowly, you'll make me fall.

211
00:11:59,288 --> 00:12:02,928
- Hey, close the umbrella. - Why would you open it indoors?

212
00:12:05,328 --> 00:12:06,598
Are you both ready?

213
00:12:08,738 --> 00:12:12,638
Wow. You look so handsome today.

214
00:12:12,768 --> 00:12:15,408
Of course. When I was young,

215
00:12:15,578 --> 00:12:18,308
I was often told I looked like Shin Sung Il.

216
00:12:18,948 --> 00:12:22,078
Thank you for preparing the food in my place.

217
00:12:22,478 --> 00:12:24,348
I was originally going to do it all myself.

218
00:12:24,488 --> 00:12:25,488
Don't be silly.

219
00:12:25,548 --> 00:12:27,988
You've been doing the hard prep work for days.

220
00:12:29,358 --> 00:12:31,728
You look beautiful. You too, Mom.

221
00:12:32,328 --> 00:12:36,128
- Shall we go? - Yes. Come on, Lee Young Hwa.

222
00:12:36,528 --> 00:12:38,098
Here, take my arm.

223
00:12:40,138 --> 00:12:42,498
- My gosh. - Oh, dear. What's wrong?

224
00:12:42,568 --> 00:12:43,568
Oh, it hurts.

225
00:12:43,638 --> 00:12:47,008
Oh, my, are you okay? What do we do? Oh, my.

226
00:12:47,078 --> 00:12:49,778
- All of a sudden... - Oh, my.

227
00:12:49,838 --> 00:12:51,048
Oh, honey.

228
00:12:51,808 --> 00:12:52,808
Oh, honey.

229
00:12:55,078 --> 00:12:57,718
- I need to use the restroom... - Yes.

230
00:13:00,458 --> 00:13:01,588
Oh no, what do I do?

231
00:13:02,158 --> 00:13:03,258
Oh dear, what do I do?

232
00:13:03,658 --> 00:13:06,088
Arrange the flowers nicely over here.

233
00:13:06,158 --> 00:13:08,458
- Here you go, Eun Ae. - Okay.

234
00:13:09,158 --> 00:13:12,068
Well, it looks like we're all ready. Has everyone practised enough?

235
00:13:12,228 --> 00:13:14,568
Practice? I'll just follow along.

236
00:13:14,798 --> 00:13:16,838
Me too. Manager Seo, please lead the way.

237
00:13:17,168 --> 00:13:18,168
Do we have to do a good job?

238
00:13:18,238 --> 00:13:20,078
As long as the Chairman is happy, that's all that matters.

239
00:13:20,778 --> 00:13:21,938
Okay, let's give it our all until the end.

240
00:13:22,208 --> 00:13:23,208
Yes.

241
00:13:24,108 --> 00:13:26,918
- How are you feeling? - Oh, I'm great.

242
00:13:27,378 --> 00:13:29,318
Thanks to the dreamcatcher and this bracelet...

243
00:13:29,378 --> 00:13:31,088
you gave me, Eun Ae, I slept very well.

244
00:13:31,748 --> 00:13:32,748
Me too.

245
00:13:35,258 --> 00:13:37,388
- Such a good photographer. - She's really pretty.

246
00:13:37,458 --> 00:13:40,358
- Bit Na, take a picture of us too. - Okay.

247
00:13:40,998 --> 00:13:42,598
One, two, three.

248
00:13:44,628 --> 00:13:45,628
Did it turn out well?

249
00:13:46,128 --> 00:13:49,368
Oh my goodness. Is this a house or an amusement park?

250
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:52,138
These beautiful trees, every single flower,

251
00:13:52,208 --> 00:13:53,508
and every blade of grass...

252
00:13:53,938 --> 00:13:56,738
- I've tended to them with my hands. - Is that so?

253
00:13:56,808 --> 00:13:58,648
Grandma, hurry. Everyone's waiting.

254
00:13:58,708 --> 00:14:00,848
- Right. - Aunt Cho Rong.

255
00:14:00,918 --> 00:14:03,548
- Bit Na. - Oh, Bit Na.

256
00:14:03,918 --> 00:14:06,288
Wow, you look amazing in that suit.

257
00:14:06,548 --> 00:14:09,118
- A rich family's youngest son. - Oh, come on.

258
00:14:09,418 --> 00:14:10,828
- The original mung bean pancake? - Yes.

259
00:14:10,888 --> 00:14:11,888
Let me help you with one of those.

260
00:14:12,488 --> 00:14:13,498
Bit Na, let's go too.

261
00:14:14,458 --> 00:14:15,458
Bit Na, wait up.

262
00:14:43,588 --> 00:14:46,128
You look so beautiful, Bung Nim.

263
00:14:46,628 --> 00:14:48,958
What are you talking about? I was up all night writing,

264
00:14:49,228 --> 00:14:50,868
and I barely had time to wash my face before coming out.

265
00:14:51,368 --> 00:14:53,838
You look good in a suit too, Bung Woo.

266
00:15:01,008 --> 00:15:02,308
- Assistant Manager Kim. - Yes.

267
00:15:02,378 --> 00:15:04,678
Put the lid on this properly. Dust is getting in.

268
00:15:04,748 --> 00:15:06,778
One, two, three. One, two, three. Mic test.

269
00:15:06,848 --> 00:15:10,018
Honey, you look so professional.

270
00:15:10,078 --> 00:15:12,148
How do I look today? Like the goddess of the party?

271
00:15:12,688 --> 00:15:16,458
Crystal, please restrain yourself. Today's star is my father.

272
00:15:16,518 --> 00:15:19,688
- Not you, my father. Remember that. - I know.

273
00:15:21,458 --> 00:15:22,498
Check, one, two.

274
00:15:23,568 --> 00:15:24,898
Why aren't they coming out yet?

275
00:15:25,398 --> 00:15:26,468
I wonder if something happened.

276
00:15:26,728 --> 00:15:28,768
I know. Maybe I should go in and check.

277
00:15:28,838 --> 00:15:32,038
No, honey. Kang Yeon Ja said she would bring him out.

278
00:15:32,138 --> 00:15:33,138
Let's wait.

279
00:15:43,378 --> 00:15:47,118
You shouldn't push yourself. We can still cancel. Okay?

280
00:15:48,018 --> 00:15:49,758
I'll call Dr. Kim.

281
00:15:50,058 --> 00:15:51,328
What are you talking about?

282
00:15:53,228 --> 00:15:55,028
The guests I invited...

283
00:15:55,658 --> 00:16:00,298
- I can't just send them away. - You can invite them next time.

284
00:16:00,768 --> 00:16:03,398
Right now, you need to think about your health first.

285
00:16:05,638 --> 00:16:07,678
There won't be a next time.

286
00:16:09,808 --> 00:16:12,308
I'm really okay now.

287
00:16:14,818 --> 00:16:17,288
- Let's go, Yeon Soon. - Yes, Chairman.

288
00:16:28,198 --> 00:16:31,998
(My Happy Funeral)

289
00:16:35,398 --> 00:16:36,738
Chairman.

290
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:42,738
(My Happy Funeral)

291
00:16:45,548 --> 00:16:47,478
All right, everyone, please take your seats.

292
00:16:48,648 --> 00:16:49,918
Let's sit.

293
00:16:50,418 --> 00:16:51,488
Just sit down.

294
00:16:52,918 --> 00:16:56,318
My beloved father, Chairman Ko Gang Su's...

295
00:16:56,718 --> 00:16:58,228
living funeral...

296
00:16:59,288 --> 00:17:00,428
will now begin.

297
00:17:03,258 --> 00:17:04,798
(My Happy Funeral)

298
00:17:04,898 --> 00:17:06,128
Now, a round of applause, please.

299
00:17:06,668 --> 00:17:08,798
Great-grandfather, please stay healthy...

300
00:17:08,868 --> 00:17:10,068
for a long, long time.

301
00:17:10,468 --> 00:17:13,268
Yes. For my great-granddaughter's sake,

302
00:17:13,338 --> 00:17:16,408
I will live a long and healthy life.

303
00:17:21,578 --> 00:17:22,648
Next,

304
00:17:23,018 --> 00:17:26,248
we will hear from our Chairman, Ko Gang Su.

305
00:17:29,558 --> 00:17:32,888
(My Happy Funeral)

306
00:17:35,158 --> 00:17:37,568
I'm sure you're all puzzled.

307
00:17:38,798 --> 00:17:41,938
Seeing me walk in here on the day of my own funeral.

308
00:17:44,338 --> 00:17:48,078
I created this gathering because I wanted...

309
00:17:48,638 --> 00:17:52,148
to shake hands and share a meal with all of you,

310
00:17:52,808 --> 00:18:00,218
and to share a joyful and happy farewell.

311
00:18:01,818 --> 00:18:04,488
Please, feel free to eat and drink.

312
00:18:05,158 --> 00:18:11,268
I hope you all have a fun and pleasant time today.

313
00:18:14,598 --> 00:18:19,668
Thank you for being a part of my life.

314
00:18:19,968 --> 00:18:21,978
(My Happy Funeral)

315
00:18:22,038 --> 00:18:23,038
Thanks to all of you,

316
00:18:24,208 --> 00:18:26,178
it has been a wonderful life.

317
00:18:33,918 --> 00:18:36,288
(My Happy Funeral)

318
00:18:36,618 --> 00:18:38,228
All right. Well...

319
00:18:39,188 --> 00:18:41,798
Thank you, Chairman Ko Gang Su, for those words.

320
00:18:43,058 --> 00:18:45,828
- Next up... - What's this about a program?

321
00:18:46,298 --> 00:18:49,238
We should just eat and drink as we please. That's all.

322
00:18:50,508 --> 00:18:51,538
Excuse me, Chairman.

323
00:18:51,608 --> 00:18:54,208
It seems your grandchildren have prepared something.

324
00:18:54,608 --> 00:18:55,738
You should see what they've prepared.

325
00:18:56,778 --> 00:18:57,878
Should I?

326
00:18:57,948 --> 00:19:00,078
(My Happy Funeral)

327
00:19:00,148 --> 00:19:01,478
Yes, for our next item,

328
00:19:01,948 --> 00:19:04,418
Chairman Ko Gang Su's second grandson...

329
00:19:05,048 --> 00:19:09,288
has personally prepared a video. Let's take a look together.

330
00:19:09,588 --> 00:19:11,328
- A video? - There's a video?

331
00:19:13,188 --> 00:19:14,198
Eun Ae.

332
00:19:16,328 --> 00:19:18,868
(To My Beloved Grandfather…)

333
00:19:28,578 --> 00:19:29,608
So he did prepare something.

334
00:19:31,008 --> 00:19:32,378
(Gangsu Construction)

335
00:19:33,078 --> 00:19:34,078
Oh my.

336
00:19:35,948 --> 00:19:37,288
Oh my, how dashing.

337
00:19:38,148 --> 00:19:39,248
Oh my.

338
00:19:39,848 --> 00:19:41,758
(Gangsu Construction Apartment Construction Site)

339
00:19:43,058 --> 00:19:44,458
Oh my, look.

340
00:20:09,078 --> 00:20:12,218
Like two lovebirds. My, they look wonderful.

341
00:20:12,588 --> 00:20:13,818
They look so wonderful together.

342
00:20:27,868 --> 00:20:30,538
Grandfather. It's your eldest grandson, Min Ho.

343
00:20:31,738 --> 00:20:34,278
When I was young, I caused so much trouble...

344
00:20:34,538 --> 00:20:36,038
and was such a troublemaker.

345
00:20:36,578 --> 00:20:39,278
But with your stern advice and tough love,

346
00:20:39,748 --> 00:20:41,948
I've finally started to mature.

347
00:20:42,278 --> 00:20:44,318
Though I still have a long way to go.

348
00:20:46,148 --> 00:20:48,018
Until I'm completely grown up,

349
00:20:48,318 --> 00:20:49,888
please stay by my side for a long, long time.

350
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:52,628
I love you, Grandfather.

351
00:20:54,058 --> 00:20:55,058
Chairman.

352
00:20:55,558 --> 00:20:59,268
The first time I met you, I think I was six years old.

353
00:20:59,898 --> 00:21:01,868
Even though we lived in the same house,

354
00:21:01,938 --> 00:21:03,738
I never got to call you Grandfather,

355
00:21:04,368 --> 00:21:05,938
and that's my biggest regret now.

356
00:21:07,068 --> 00:21:08,638
The next time I see you,

357
00:21:09,278 --> 00:21:11,308
I want to call you Grandfather too.

358
00:21:12,178 --> 00:21:13,408
You'll let me, won't you?

359
00:21:15,518 --> 00:21:17,748
Please live a long and healthy life.

360
00:21:19,488 --> 00:21:21,818
Hello, Chairman. It's me, Eun Ae.

361
00:21:22,258 --> 00:21:25,228
Thank you again for never giving up on finding my mother.

362
00:21:25,588 --> 00:21:27,188
I'm so grateful to you.

363
00:21:27,658 --> 00:21:31,168
We will properly complete the Retirement Community project...

364
00:21:31,228 --> 00:21:32,228
as you wished,

365
00:21:32,298 --> 00:21:33,668
so please watch over us until the end.

366
00:21:34,138 --> 00:21:35,398
I love you, Grandfather.

367
00:21:36,468 --> 00:21:38,538
Okay, now it's your turn, Team Leader Ko. Come on.

368
00:21:38,608 --> 00:21:40,538
(Strategic Planning Division)

369
00:21:45,578 --> 00:21:46,578
Grandfather.

370
00:21:47,778 --> 00:21:49,348
If you weren't in my life,

371
00:21:50,048 --> 00:21:51,648
where would I be right now?

372
00:21:52,818 --> 00:21:55,458
Would I have ever been able to achieve my dream?

373
00:21:57,328 --> 00:22:00,258
You brought me into this world,

374
00:22:01,098 --> 00:22:02,428
helped me get back on my feet,

375
00:22:03,228 --> 00:22:04,268
and...

376
00:22:05,128 --> 00:22:08,238
you gave me a reason to live again.

377
00:22:09,498 --> 00:22:11,308
All the love you've given me...

378
00:22:12,508 --> 00:22:14,008
I want to repay even a little of it,

379
00:22:16,078 --> 00:22:18,248
so please grant me plenty of time.

380
00:22:19,948 --> 00:22:21,048
I'm so grateful,

381
00:22:21,818 --> 00:22:22,848
and I love you.

382
00:22:23,378 --> 00:22:24,388
Grandfather.

383
00:22:31,628 --> 00:22:33,158
(Grandfather, We Respect And Love You)

384
00:22:34,798 --> 00:22:37,428
- Oh my. - Thank you all.

385
00:22:37,968 --> 00:22:40,568
When did you all make that?

386
00:22:41,198 --> 00:22:42,698
You must have been so busy with work.

387
00:22:44,708 --> 00:22:47,578
That was a very touching video you all prepared.

388
00:22:48,608 --> 00:22:49,808
Next on the program,

389
00:22:50,678 --> 00:22:52,548
we will have a gift presentation.

390
00:22:53,208 --> 00:22:54,618
The one presenting the gift is...

391
00:22:54,978 --> 00:22:58,118
Now, now. I thought I told you my list of prohibitions.

392
00:22:58,388 --> 00:23:02,988
Tears, condolence money, gifts, wreaths, and mourning clothes.

393
00:23:06,228 --> 00:23:07,698
Now, everyone,

394
00:23:08,498 --> 00:23:09,498
let's enjoy ourselves.

395
00:23:10,058 --> 00:23:12,528
Eat, drink, and have a good time.

396
00:23:14,168 --> 00:23:15,197
Let's go.

397
00:23:15,198 --> 00:23:16,198
- Let's go eat. - Go ahead.

398
00:23:16,199 --> 00:23:17,908
- Let's go. - Come on, let's go eat.

399
00:23:17,968 --> 00:23:20,038
- Ma'am. - Here.

400
00:23:21,008 --> 00:23:22,878
- Let's eat. - Here you go.

401
00:23:24,548 --> 00:23:25,548
Here.

402
00:23:32,448 --> 00:23:35,288
Hey, why have you had that look on your face this whole time?

403
00:23:35,958 --> 00:23:37,828
- Are you sick? - No, sir.

404
00:23:38,088 --> 00:23:39,288
You sure don't look fine.

405
00:23:39,988 --> 00:23:43,028
Hey, if you're not feeling well, just go home. Don't ruin the mood.

406
00:23:43,798 --> 00:23:46,298
You go on. I'll get some air and come back inside.

407
00:23:46,398 --> 00:23:47,568
All right. I'm going.

408
00:23:48,638 --> 00:23:50,498
You need to get that look off your face.

409
00:23:52,268 --> 00:23:54,638
People will think something is wrong.

410
00:23:55,138 --> 00:23:57,677
What are you doing out here?

411
00:23:57,678 --> 00:23:58,978
Oh, you startled me.

412
00:23:59,478 --> 00:24:01,748
Why? Have a guilty conscience?

413
00:24:01,818 --> 00:24:04,618
- What's to be startled about? - What do you mean, guilty?

414
00:24:06,118 --> 00:24:08,818
Nice outfit. Very retro. Year 2000.

415
00:24:09,288 --> 00:24:10,888
Year 2000? That's nonsense.

416
00:24:12,758 --> 00:24:15,358
What's wrong? You look awfully pale.

417
00:24:16,658 --> 00:24:19,268
It's nothing, sir. I just didn't sleep well last night.

418
00:24:22,368 --> 00:24:23,438
What's with him?

419
00:24:23,938 --> 00:24:26,768
He seemed startled when he saw Manager Han's picture earlier.

420
00:24:28,738 --> 00:24:29,738
What?

421
00:24:30,308 --> 00:24:31,848
Is it time for some drinking and singing?

422
00:24:47,088 --> 00:24:51,568
- You are so beautiful - Crystal, hurry up!

423
00:24:51,628 --> 00:24:55,638
You shine brighter than starlight in the night sky

424
00:24:56,138 --> 00:24:58,508
- My weary heart - My weary heart

425
00:24:58,568 --> 00:25:01,278
- That will warmly embrace - That will warmly embrace

426
00:25:01,538 --> 00:25:05,148
- Your embrace is my home - Your embrace is my home

427
00:25:05,208 --> 00:25:07,578
- Here. - Before the fierce wind

428
00:25:07,648 --> 00:25:10,678
- He's so handsome. - Even my love, about to go out

429
00:25:10,948 --> 00:25:14,488
You endured and overcame it all.

430
00:25:15,488 --> 00:25:18,288
- It brings me to tears - Honey, us too.

431
00:25:18,358 --> 00:25:20,798
Do you know how grateful I am

432
00:25:20,998 --> 00:25:24,728
- That you are by my side? - Cho Rong.

433
00:25:25,128 --> 00:25:29,598
- I love you, I love you - I love you, I love you

434
00:25:29,998 --> 00:25:34,738
I know I may not be good enough for you

435
00:25:35,008 --> 00:25:39,948
And we may get tired as the years go by

436
00:25:40,348 --> 00:25:43,948
But I will be your resting place

437
00:25:44,588 --> 00:25:48,988
- I love you, my precious love - I love you, my precious love

438
00:25:49,458 --> 00:25:51,728
- This song I will sing only for you - This song I will sing only for you

439
00:25:51,788 --> 00:25:53,958
- For the rest of my life - For the rest of my life

440
00:25:54,328 --> 00:25:58,928
- Let's sing this love song - Let's sing this love song

441
00:25:59,168 --> 00:26:03,638
- The two of us, la la la - The two of us, la la la

442
00:26:20,858 --> 00:26:21,858
Yes.

443
00:26:22,788 --> 00:26:24,728
Jeongbin Police Station, Traffic Investigation Unit?

444
00:26:26,358 --> 00:26:27,358
What?

445
00:26:27,928 --> 00:26:28,928
You found it?

446
00:26:34,068 --> 00:26:35,068
Honey.

447
00:26:35,768 --> 00:26:36,938
Seriously.

448
00:26:37,838 --> 00:26:40,838
(My Happy Funeral)

449
00:26:46,778 --> 00:26:47,778
What is wrong with you?

450
00:26:47,779 --> 00:26:49,517
You should humour my father on a day like today.

451
00:26:49,518 --> 00:26:50,648
Go on already.

452
00:26:51,818 --> 00:26:53,888
Why are you two acting like this? It's a special day.

453
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:06,128
Dad...

454
00:27:56,478 --> 00:27:59,388
(Our Happy Days)

455
00:27:59,488 --> 00:28:01,118
I mean, isn't this absurd?

456
00:28:01,618 --> 00:28:02,788
The mother takes the daughter's place,

457
00:28:02,858 --> 00:28:03,988
and the daughter takes the daughter-in-law's place.

458
00:28:04,058 --> 00:28:05,958
- Doesn't it feel like a drama? - A drama?

459
00:28:06,028 --> 00:28:07,188
Three families, all tangled together.

460
00:28:07,258 --> 00:28:08,858
Coincidence becomes inevitable, and then destiny?

461
00:28:08,958 --> 00:28:11,168
What if there's a massive secret hidden between our three families...

462
00:28:11,228 --> 00:28:12,328
that we don't know about?

463
00:28:12,398 --> 00:28:13,928
This is so entertaining. Keep going.

464
00:28:13,998 --> 00:28:16,198
You two? Absolutely not. There is a proper order to things.

465
00:28:16,268 --> 00:28:17,738
We have absolutely no intention of breaking up.

466
00:28:17,808 --> 00:28:20,068
Oh, my goodness. This is ridiculous.

467
00:28:20,138 --> 00:28:22,238
Instead of us giving our consent to Gyeol,

468
00:28:22,308 --> 00:28:25,108
what if Kang Yeon Ja lets go of what she is holding on to?

469
00:28:31,688 --> 00:28:34,518
(Our Happy Days)
